<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Grootvlei gold mine may cut jobs.</title>
<headline>Grootvlei gold mine may cut jobs.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grootvlei Proprietary Mines Ltd said on Tuesday that &quot;some fairly drastic measures&quot; were needed to return it profitability, including possible job losses.  </p>
<p>The company said it had invited union representatives to a meeting on June 26 to discuss the mine's financial difficulties.</p>
<p>General manager Neal Fronemen said Grootvlei had been hit by a lower gold price, rising costs and reduced output, compounded by a shortfall of 11 million rand between its pumping costs and its government subsidy over the next financial year.</p>
<p>Various ways of cutting costs were being evaluated.</p>
<p>&quot;This may involve retrenchment or redundancy of a number of employees,&quot; Froneman said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
